  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Chicago Poker. Seven Card Stud, split pot. 2-8 players. 2 down, 1 up; 4th-6th up, 7th down. Five betting rounds. Pot splits 50/50: best 5-card hand wins half, highest face-down spade wins half. Must have spade in hole to win spade half. Variants: Low Chicago (lowest spade), Follow the Queen, etc.',
    Player: "Welcome to Chicago Poker! This Seven Card Stud variant splits the pot—half to the best hand, half to the highest SPADE IN THE HOLE. Face-up spades don't count! Watch your opponents' upcards to track which spades might still be hidden. Can you balance building a strong hand with hunting for that Ace of Spades in the hole",
    objective: 'Win half the pot with the highest poker hand OR win half the pot by holding the highest spade in the hole (face-down cards only).',
    gameplay: '1. **Ante**: All players post an ante. 2. **Initial Deal**: Each player receives 2 cards face down and 1 card face up. 3. **Bring-in**: Player with the lowest upcard posts a compulsory bring-in bet (or highest in some variants). 4. **Betting Rounds**: Five rounds of betting follow each card dealt (after 3rd, 4th, 5th, 6th, and 7th streets). 5. **Declaration**: After final betting, active players declare whether they are going for High Hand, High Spade, or Both.',
    keyRules: [
      'Pot is split 50/50 between best poker hand and highest spade in the hole (High Chicago).',
      'Only FACE-DOWN spades count for the spade half of the pot.',
      'If the Ace of Spades is dealt face up, the King of Spades in the hole becomes the best possible spade.',
      'Declaration can be sequential (around the table) or simultaneous (chips in fist: 1=High Hand, 2=High Spade, 3=Both).',
      'To win the spade half, you MUST have a spade face down. Without one, you cannot win that half even if no one else declares spade.',
      "Declaring 'Both' requires winning BOTH halves to win anything (Pig Rule in some variants).",
    ],
